WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.398
CCS is described by two statistics along the probe
direction: sigma-d-squared,

00:00:05.478 --> 00:00:10.665
how far a statement and its negation are pushed
apart, and sigma-m-squared,

00:00:10.745 --> 00:00:13.474
how far their midpoint sits from origin.

00:00:13.554 --> 00:00:17.547
Its saturating sigmoid forces a trade-off between the two.

00:00:17.627 --> 00:00:22.041
Midpoint-Displacement makes this explicit with one
knob, lambda,

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:24.780
reproducing CCS or maximizing accuracy.
